mithril (0.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * --keys: recover near-zero EC private scalars by a bounded d*G==Q search,
    detecting the October 2026 eMudhra P-384 CA compromise (P-256/384/521 and
    secp256k1); the eight real eMudhra intermediates are fingerprinted.
  * --cve: on an interactive terminal with no local mirror, offer to download
    it before scanning. New --no-fetch (and MITHRIL_NO_FETCH) suppress the
    offer; non-interactive runs still error as before.
  * CLI: breaking flag renames for coherence. --component-cves-all is now
    --component-cves-full and --kernel-cves-all is now --kernel-cves-full
    ("all" means all passes; "full" means all detail within a pass). New --full
    for maximum human detail. --help is regrouped; JSON is always complete.
  * SBOM: recover components from monolithic non-ELF firmware. Document that
    -C/--outdir also writes sbom.cdx.json and sbom.spdx.json.

 -- Matt Brown <matt@brownfinesecurity.com>  Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:09:46 -0400

mithril (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New --boot Boot Security pass: U-Boot env, device tree, and FIT posture.
  * New --keys Public-Key Weakness pass (batch-GCD shared-prime detection).
  * UEFI variable stores and Secure Boot certificate/dbx enumeration, including
    standalone variable stores that carry no firmware-volume header.
  * Precision fixes: PEM private-key bodies, GPL-vs-LGPL identification,
    generic-secret false positives, vendor-fork CVE ranges, JSON number parsing.

 -- Matt Brown <matt@brownfinesecurity.com>  Mon, 05 Oct 2026 13:01:08 -0400

